  "passage": "Alex is a 15-year-old student at Riverdale High School. He is very creative and enjoys swimming in his free time. His art teacher, Mrs. Brown, often praises his original ideas. Last week, she assigned the class to draw an accurate picture of the historic cathedral in town. Alex decided to ride his scooter there to get the best view. While he was sketching, he noticed a man acting strangely near the bridge. The man seemed to be planning something. Alex remembered that sometimes criminals use such places for illegal activities. He quickly called the police. The officers arrived and arrested the man, who was indeed trying to steal jewellery from a tourist shop. Alex's quick action was highlighted in the local newspaper. For instance, his story encouraged other students to be more aware of their surroundings. Alex says, 'It's important to use your skills for good. Though I was scared, I knew I had to help.'",
